    "Heights are the A/B values of bible 5.1; in Unity TerrainBaker scales each tree to its plan height (5.3), so the model height only fixes proportions.",
    "Gradients: grad.leaf (linden, poplar), grad.birch (one step lighter), grad.conifer (spruce, pine).",
    "LOD1 (bible 5.2.7) is not part of v01/v02.",
    "v02: linden and pine crowns are ONE smooth surface (smooth union of template ellipsoids projected onto a geodesic sphere, 500 / 320 even triangles, smooth normals) instead of intersecting lobes; poplars stand upright; the pine trunk is stout and its crown clusters at the top.",
    "v02b (2026-10-07, critique of the trial frame): geodesic vertices keyed by exact barycentric weights (the freq-5 crowns of v02 test builds had 32 open edges); pine crown bottom back to bible 5.1 (7.0 / 5.5 m, trunk visible on 55 %) with 3 cushions + a dome clustered in the top 45 %.",
    "The .blend shows the assets in rows along +X; every FBX has its root at the origin."
